Q: How to pretty print the DB statement on debug level? A: <p>I ran into the same issue.</p>
<p>Since I'm using the <code>tracing</code> crate, I fixed it by creating a custom layer.</p>
<pre class="lang-rust prettyprint-override"><code>
struct PrettySqlLayer;

impl&lt;S: Subscriber&gt; Layer&lt;S&gt; for PrettySqlLayer {
    fn on_event(&amp;self, event: &amp;Event&lt;'_&gt;, _ctx: Context&lt;'_, S&gt;) {
        if event.metadata().target() != &quot;sqlx::query&quot; {
            return;
        }

        #[derive(Default)]
        struct V {
            statement: Option&lt;String&gt;,
            summary: Option&lt;String&gt;,
        }
        impl Visit for V {
            fn record_str(&amp;mut self, field: &amp;Field, value: &amp;str) {
                match field.name() {
                    &quot;db.statement&quot; =&gt; self.statement = Some(value.to_string()),
                    &quot;summary&quot; =&gt; self.summary = Some(value.to_string()),
                    _ =&gt; {}
                }
            }
            fn record_debug(&amp;mut self, field: &amp;Field, value: &amp;dyn std::fmt::Debug) {
                if field.name() == &quot;db.statement&quot; {
                    let raw = format!(&quot;{:?}&quot;, value);
                    self.statement = Some(
                        raw.trim_matches('&quot;')
                            .replace(&quot;\\n&quot;, &quot;\n&quot;)
                            .replace(&quot;\\t&quot;, &quot;  &quot;),
                    );
                }
            }
        }

        let mut v = V::default();
        event.record(&amp;mut v);

        if let Some(sql) = v.statement {
            let sql = sql
                .lines()
                .filter(|l| !l.trim().is_empty())
                .collect::&lt;Vec&lt;_&gt;&gt;()
                .join(&quot;\n&quot;);
            println!(&quot;\nsummery: \x1b[36m {}\x1b[0m\n{}&quot;, v.summary.unwrap_or_default(), sql);
        }
    }
</code></pre>
<p>Add this layer to subscriber</p>
<pre class="lang-rust prettyprint-override"><code>    let subscriber = tracing_subscriber::registry()
        .with(into_file_subscriber)
        .with(into_stdout_subscriber)
        .with(PrettySqlLayer);
</code></pre>
<p>Output:</p>
<pre><code>25.07.2026 16:26:10.607 DEBUG sqlx::query: summary=&quot;select r.id, r.name, r.description, …&quot; db.statement=&quot;\n\nselect r.id, r.name, r.description, r.created_at from roles as r where r.name = $1\n&quot; rows_affected=1 rows_returned=1 elapsed=1.469662ms elapsed_secs=0.001469662

summery:  select r.id, r.name, r.description, …
select r.id, r.name, r.description, r.created_at from roles as r where r.name = $1
</code></pre>

